From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yu Zhang(Yuriy) <yu.zhang@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Oct 2026 11:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] FIXUP: arm64: dts: qcom: nord-ride-embedded: Add WCN DIG
 rail on GPIO7

Per the Ride Embedded schematic, PMIC E GPIO7 enables a 1.9V rail (1.8-2.1V range)
that feeds the WCN7850 VDD_DIG domain. Describe that rail and point
vdddig-supply at it so the power sequencer enables it as part of the
WLAN power-up, instead of sharing the 0.95V core rail.

Signed-off-by: Yu Zhang(Yuriy) <yu.zhang@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261021022921.2053957-5-shengchao.guo@oss.qualcomm.com/]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/nord-ride-embedded.dts | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/nord-ride-embedded.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/nord-ride-embedded.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/nord-ride-embedded.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/nord-ride-embedded.dts
@@ -83,6 +83,15 @@
 		enable-active-high;
 	};

+	vreg_wcn_1p9: regulator-wcn-1p9 {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "vreg_wcn_1p9";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <1900000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <1900000>;
+		gpio = <&pmau0102_e_gpios 7 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+	};
+
 	vreg_wcn_core_vl_0p95: regulator-wcn-core-vl-0p95 {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		regulator-name = "vreg_wcn_core_vl_0p95";
@@ -118,7 +127,7 @@
 		vdd-supply = <&vreg_wcn_3p3>;
 		vddio-supply = <&vreg_s3a_1p8>;
 		vddaon-supply = <&vreg_wcn_core_vl_0p95>;
-		vdddig-supply = <&vreg_wcn_core_vl_0p95>;
+		vdddig-supply = <&vreg_wcn_1p9>;
 		vddrfa1p2-supply = <&vreg_wcn_core_vm_1p35>;
 		vddrfa1p8-supply = <&vreg_wcn_core_vh_1p95>;
 
--
2.34.1
